---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
const desc = 'Free colocation cost calculator: monthly and annual cost of cabinets, committed power, overage and cross-connects, with an effective cost per kW and per rack.';
const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Colocation Cost Calculator', applicationCategory: 'BusinessApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Web', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  url: 'https://theworldofai.org/calculators/colocation-cost/',
});

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is colocation billed on space or on power?',
    a: 'On power, in every high-density deal and most conventional ones. A cabinet rate buys a footprint and a small power allowance, typically a few kilowatts, and everything above that allowance is billed per kilowatt. At AI densities the power line dwarfs the space line.' },
  { q: 'What is the difference between committed and metered power?',
    a: 'Committed power is billed on the capacity reserved, whether or not it is drawn. Metered is billed on actual consumption. Commitment is the more common structure for high density because the provider has to build and hold the capacity either way. Which one a contract uses changes the arithmetic completely, and it is worth confirming before comparing two quotes.' },
  { q: 'Why are cross-connects so expensive for what they are?',
    a: 'A cross-connect is a physical cable between two cabinets in the same building, and it is priced on the value of the interconnection rather than the cost of the cable. In carrier-dense facilities it is what customers are paying for, and recurring cross-connect revenue is a significant share of a colocation operator margin.' },
  { q: 'What is not in this calculator that will be on the invoice?',
    a: 'Annual escalators, commonly around 3 percent compounding over a multi-year term. Remote hands, billed hourly. Power circuit installation fees per circuit. Bandwidth or IP transit if bought from the provider. Cancellation and early-termination terms. Over a five-year deal the escalator alone can add more than a tenth of the total.' },
  { q: 'Can I get AI racks on a standard rate card?',
    a: 'Usually not. Standard cabinet products assume 5 to 10 kW; racks at 40 kW and above need dedicated power distribution, containment or liquid cooling, and often a different part of the building. Those deals are quoted individually, priced per kilowatt rather than per cabinet, and the lead time on capacity is frequently the binding constraint rather than the price.' },
];
---
<Base title="Colocation Cost Calculator: monthly space, power and cross-connects — The World of AI" description={desc} current="/calculators/" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <h1>Colocation Cost Calculator</h1>
  <p class="answer">Colocation is billed on committed power far more than on floor space. A cabinet rents for a monthly fee that includes a power allowance; kilowatts beyond it are billed per kW committed, whether or not they are drawn, and cross-connects are charged per circuit per month.</p>
  <p class="meta-line">Formula and defaults last reviewed: 2026-08-31.</p>

  <div class="calc">
    <label>Cabinets <input type="number" id="cabs" value="20" step="1" min="1" /></label>
    <label>Cabinet rate ($ per cabinet per month) <input type="number" id="cabrate" value="900" step="50" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Power included per cabinet (kW) <input type="number" id="incl" value="5" step="0.5" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Power drawn per cabinet (kW) <input type="number" id="draw" value="8" step="0.5" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Committed power rate ($ per kW per month) <input type="number" id="kwrate" value="150" step="5" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Cross-connects <input type="number" id="xc" value="8" step="1" min="0" /></label>
    <label>Cross-connect ($ each per month) <input type="number" id="xcrate" value="300" step="25" min="0" /></label>
    <label>One-off install and setup ($) <input type="number" id="setup" value="25000" step="1000" min="0" /></label>
    <div class="out" id="out" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </div>

  <h2>How the math works</h2>
  <p>Monthly = cabinets × cabinet rate, plus power drawn above the included allowance × the
    per-kW rate, plus cross-connects × their rate. The power line is the one that surprises
    people: at 8 kW a cabinet with a 5 kW allowance, power is often the largest single item on
    the invoice.</p>
  <h2>What to check in the contract, not the calculator</h2>
  <p>Whether power is billed on commitment or on metered draw changes the arithmetic entirely,
    and commitment is the more common structure for high density. Ask whether the rate is per kW
    of UPS capacity or of utility feed, whether redundancy is A+B and how each feed is billed,
    and what the escalator is: a 3% annual uplift over a five-year term is a real cost this
    calculator does not model. High-density AI cabinets are also frequently quoted outside
    standard rate cards altogether.</p>

  <h2>What does a twenty cabinet footprint cost?</h2>
  <p>Twenty cabinets at $900 a month, 5 kW included each, drawing 8 kW each, committed power at
    $150 per kW per month, eight cross-connects at $300, and $25,000 of one-off install.</p>
  <p>Space is 20 × $900, or $18,000. Power above allowance is 3 kW per cabinet across 20 cabinets,
    which is 60 kW, at $150, or $9,000. Cross-connects are $2,400. The month is $29,400 and the
    year is $352,800; with setup, year one is $377,800. Across 160 kW total draw that is $184 per
    kW per month, or $1,470 per cabinet.</p>
  <p>Space is 61 percent of that monthly bill at 8 kW a cabinet. Raise the draw to 15 kW and power
    becomes $30,000 against $18,000 of space, and the deal is a power contract with some floor
    attached.</p>

  <h2>Colocation or build?</h2>
  <p>The comparison people get wrong is against the energy calculator's output rather than against
    the whole cost of ownership. At $184 per kW per month, this deal is about $2,200 per kW a year.
    Powering the same load in an owned facility, on the energy calculator's defaults, is about $962
    per kW a year, so colocation looks like double.</p>
  <p>It is not, because that $962 is electricity alone. The owned case also carries the building,
    the electrical and mechanical plant, redundancy, maintenance, staffing and the capital tied up
    in all of it, none of which appears in an energy figure. The honest comparison is total cost of
    ownership per kilowatt over the asset life, and the answer usually turns on scale and on how
    certain the demand forecast is: colocation buys optionality, and a build buys unit economics
    that only pay back if the capacity is actually filled.</p>

  <Faq items={faqs} />

  <div class="cite-box">Cite this tool: <code>"Colocation Cost Calculator." The World of AI,
    theworldofai.org/calculators/colocation-cost/.</code></div>

  <script is:inline>
  (function () {
    function n(i) { return parseFloat(document.getElementById(i).value) || 0; }
    function f(v, d) { return v.toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: d === undefined ? 0 : d }); }
    var IDS = ['cabs','cabrate','incl','draw','kwrate','xc','xcrate','setup'];
    function calc() {
      var space = n('cabs') * n('cabrate');
      var extraKw = Math.max(0, n('draw') - n('incl')) * n('cabs');
      var power = extraKw * n('kwrate');
      var xc = n('xc') * n('xcrate');
      var month = space + power + xc;
      var totalKw = n('draw') * n('cabs');
      document.getElementById('out').innerHTML =
        'Monthly: <b>$' + f(month) + '</b> &nbsp;·&nbsp; annual: <b>$' + f(month * 12) + '</b><br>' +
        'Space $' + f(space) + ' &nbsp;·&nbsp; power beyond allowance $' + f(power) + ' (' + f(extraKw, 1) + ' kW) &nbsp;·&nbsp; cross-connects $' + f(xc) + '<br>' +
        'Year one including setup: <b>$' + f(month * 12 + n('setup')) + '</b><br>' +
        '<span class="sub">Effective $' + f(totalKw > 0 ? month / totalKw : 0) + ' per kW per month across ' + f(totalKw, 1) + ' kW, or $' + f(month / (n('cabs') || 1)) + ' per cabinet.</span>';
    }
    IDS.forEach(function (i) {
      document.getElementById(i).addEventListener('input', calc);
      document.getElementById(i).addEventListener('change', calc);
    });
    calc();
  })();
  </script>
  <style>
    .calc { border: 1px solid #e6e4de; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; background: #fafaf6; margin: 1.4em 0; }
    .calc label { display: block; margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 14px; color: #26262b; }
    .calc input, .calc select { display: block; margin-top: 4px; padding: 7px 9px; font-size: 15px;
      border: 1px solid #cfcdc6; border-radius: 6px; width: 220px; max-width: 100%; }
    .out { margin-top: 14px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid #e6e4de; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .out b { color: #201868; }
    .sub { color: #7A8A9E; font-size: 13.5px; }
  </style>
</Base>
